## 4. Measurement Notes

### Wh and kWh

Watt-hours and kilowatt-hours measure electrical energy.

1 kWh = 1,000 Wh.

The measurement basis of the supplied average daily load figures has not yet been confirmed.

### kW and kWp

Kilowatts (kW) measure power capacity.

Kilowatt-peak (kWp) describes the rated peak power of a solar photovoltaic array under standard test conditions.

These units should not be treated as interchangeable.

### Battery Capacity

Battery capacity is expressed in kilowatt-hours (kWh).

The supplied values represent nominal capacity unless otherwise confirmed.

They do not independently establish usable battery capacity or actual storage performance.

## 5. Data Classification

- Supplied: Directly transcribed from available source information.
- Inferred: Interpreted from existing labels or descriptions.
- Calculated: Derived mathematically from supplied information.
- To collect: Information not currently available.
